<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Logger drop-in for the bundled single-node ClickHouse (docker compose).

  The ClickHouse image logs at trace: every query, every merge and every step
  of the embedded Keeper is written to /var/log/clickhouse-server (up to ten
  1 GB files in the container's own writable layer, not the volume) and again
  into system.text_log. On a compose install with a few dozen projects that
  is about 250 MB of log text and over a million text_log rows an hour, and
  roughly a sixth of the ClickHouse container's CPU at idle (measured for
  perf-cpu-production, 2026-10-27).

  Helm runs ClickHouse at warning already: values.yaml -> clickhouse.configuration
  (<logger><level>) for the built-in ClickHouse, and clickhouse.settings
  `logger/level` for the Altinity operator. This brings compose to the same
  level. Tests/Ops/ClickhouseLoggerLevel.test.js holds the three to one level.

  Warnings and errors are still logged, to the file and to system.text_log -
  the Admin Health page reads text_log for Warning and above only. To debug
  ClickHouse itself, raise the level in a drop-in of your own (trace, debug).

  config.d is merged into the server config, so only <logger><level> is
  replaced: the log files, their rotation and everything else stay as the
  image configures them.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <logger>
        <level>warning</level>
    </logger>
</clickhouse>
